, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 101, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": 18, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 328, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": 22, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 97, "itemDescription": "The biotech firm, known for its COVID-19 test, continued to rake in revenue for the device, making more than $3 billion off COVID-testing alone in 2022. Total revenue shot up 14.5%, nearing $45 billion.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>Thermo Fisher kicked off 2023 with its acquisition of diagnostics company The Binding Site in an all-cash transaction of $2.8 billion.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>In December 2022, the U.S. Food and Drug Administration granted emergency use authorization for Thermo Fisher\u2019s test to detect monkeypox.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>As competitors like Novartis and Biogen announced plans to cut back on R&amp;D projects in early 2023, Thermo Fisher showed signs of continued innovation. New product releases include an instrument to analyze trace elements like toxins in food and beverages as well as an automated digital tool to increase productivity in molecular research.</li><br />\r\n</ul>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2022, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 355, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 92, "itemDescription": "<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">A leading provider of life-science-related equipment and services to pharmaceutical, biotech, and government entities, Thermo Fisher Scientific rode a wave of demand in the second year of the pandemic: Among other things, companies making COVID vaccines and treatments continue to rely on its lab equipment. Revenue and profits each grew more than 20% in 2021.</span>"}, {"slug": "100-fastest-growing-companies", "title": "100 Fastest-Growing Companies", "year": 2022, "rank": 98, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2021, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 380, "itemDescription": "<span data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Thermo Fisher Scientific, which sells equipment, software, and services for scientific research, had a stellar 2020, lifted by huge demand for its products, such as PCR tests, during the pandemic. The lab supplier collected $6.6 billion in revenue during the year from sales of instruments and other products to more than 200 customers trying to develop COVID-19 vaccines and treatments. Overall revenue rose 26% to $32 billion, compared with the prior year, while profits soared 73% to $6.4 billion. Even with the COVID vaccine rush behind them, the company is thinking big with its $17.4 billion acquisition of contract research business PPD, which it announced in April.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:12673,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;10&quot;:2,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Thermo Fisher Scientific, which sells equipment, software, and services for scientific research, had a stellar 2020, lifted by huge demand for its products, such as PCR tests, during the pandemic. The lab supplier collected $6.6 billion in revenue during the year from sales of instruments and other products to more than 200 customers trying to develop COVID-19 vaccines and treatments. Overall revenue rose 26% to $32 billion, compared with the prior year, while profits soared 73% to $6.4 billion. Even with the COVID vaccine rush behind them, the company is thinking big with its $17.4 billion acquisition of contract research business PPD, which it announced in April.</span>"}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 95, "itemDescription": "<span data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Thermo Fisher Scientific, which sells equipment, software, and services for scientific research, had a stellar 2020, lifted by huge demand for its products, such as PCR tests, during the pandemic. The lab supplier collected $6.6 billion in revenue during the year from sales of instruments and other products to more than 200 customers trying to develop COVID-19 vaccines and treatments. Overall revenue rose 26% to $32 billion, compared with the prior year, while profits soared 73% to $6.4 billion. Even with the COVID vaccine rush behind them, the company is thinking big with its $17.4 billion acquisition of contract research business PPD, which it announced in April.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:12673,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;10&quot;:2,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Thermo Fisher Scientific, which sells equipment, software, and services for scientific research, had a stellar 2020, lifted by huge demand for its products, such as PCR tests, during the pandemic. The lab supplier collected $6.6 billion in revenue during the year from sales of instruments and other products to more than 200 customers trying to develop COVID-19 vaccines and treatments. Overall revenue rose 26% to $32 billion, compared with the prior year, while profits soared 73% to $6.4 billion. Even with the COVID vaccine rush behind them, the company is thinking big with its $17.4 billion acquisition of contract research business PPD, which it announced in April.</span>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2020, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 498, "itemDescription": "This manufacturer of analytical instruments, equipment, software, and services for scientific researchers has more than 75,000 employees around the world."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 119, "itemDescription": "This manufacturer of analytical instruments, equipment, software, and services for the scientific research industry has more than 75,000 employees around the world."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2019, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 124, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2018, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2018, "rank": 144, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2017, "rank": 154, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2016, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2016, "rank": 164, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2015, "rank": 181, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2014, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2014, "rank": 215, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slu